From fb03891c2f04a3f050a940a051fb7a35f7536ec3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:55:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(app): a gone plate lets go of its riders; refuse a
 45-degree turned plate

Review of PR #823:
- DeleteFixture, DeleteEntity, UntagFixture and a grid-dropping
  ImportFixture clear the direct riders' plate mounts in the same command
  (snapshotted; undo restores plate and mounts). A later plate given the
  freed name no longer carries fixtures never placed on it. Load drops
  (and logs) a place naming a plate the file does not hold.
- Detection refuses a staggered read on a plate whose edges don't run
  along X/Y (a square grid turned exactly 45 degrees); fit refusals name
  the likely cause (holes not lined up with X/Y: turned or irregular).
- Grid law: nearest holes more than a diameter apart, pitch above twice
  the 0.05 mm snap tolerance.
- MoveFixture on a plate clash-checks the riders it carries.

Pinned by fixture_plate_riders (5 tests) and
fixture_plate_detect::a_turned_plate_is_refused_naming_the_turn.

